{"stage": "step:s3", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3143, "output_tokens": 412, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "Step s3 is done. I ran the single-hit resolution simulation for the two technologies that passed the radiation requirement in s2, Sensor-T1 and Sensor-T2, at 50, 100, 150, 200 and 300 \u00b5m. Sensor-T3 was excluded because its 82% hit efficiency at 2e16 n_eq/cm\u00b2 is below the 97% requirement. All results are recorded.\n\n| Thickness (\u00b5m) | Sensor-T1 (\u00b5m) | Sensor-T2 (\u00b5m) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 50 | 10.80 | 15.42 |\n| 100 | 9.43 | 15.06 |\n| 150 | **8.92** | 14.23 |\n| 200 | 9.14 | 13.74 |\n| 300 | 11.98 | 18.40 |\n\nSensor-T1 gives the best resolution at every thickness. Its optimum is near 150 \u00b5m, at 8.92 \u00b5m. Sensor-T2 is consistently worse, with its best value of 13.74 \u00b5m at 200 \u00b5m.\n\nThese are the unirradiated resolutions from the simulation. The s2 hit efficiencies were measured at 2e16 n_eq/cm\u00b2, so the ranking at end of life is not directly checked here.", "type": "text"}]}
