{"stage": "step:s4", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2559, "output_tokens": 543, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "**Selection: Sensor-T1, planar, 150 \u00b5m thickness, single-hit resolution 8.92 \u00b5m.**\n\n**Radiation screen (2\u00d710\u00b9\u2076 neq/cm\u00b2 at end of life, requirement \u226597% hit efficiency):**\n- Sensor-T3 is excluded. Its hit efficiency is 82.0%, and full depletion is not reachable at maximum bias.\n- Sensor-T1 (98.5%) and Sensor-T2 (99.2%) both pass.\n\n**Resolution among the qualified options:**\n- **T1:** 10.80 \u00b5m (50 \u00b5m), 9.43 \u00b5m (100 \u00b5m), **8.92 \u00b5m (150 \u00b5m)**, 9.14 \u00b5m (200 \u00b5m), 11.98 \u00b5m (300 \u00b5m).\n- **T2:** 15.42 \u00b5m (50 \u00b5m) down to 13.74 \u00b5m (200 \u00b5m), rising to 18.40 \u00b5m (300 \u00b5m).\n\nThe best T2 point is about 54% worse than the best T1 point, so T2's higher radiation margin does not outweigh its resolution penalty. Within T1, the minimum sits at 150 \u00b5m. Thinner sensors lose signal and thicker ones lose charge-sharing benefit, and the simulated curve reflects that trade-off.\n\n**Documented limits:** The irradiation/test-beam report confirms the \u226597% end-of-life efficiency requirement, and T1 passes it with 1.5 points of margin. The candidate specs and meeting notes list no other numeric limits that this choice conflicts with. The notes do confirm CO\u2082 cooling at \u221235 \u00b0C, which is the operating environment assumed here.", "type": "text"}]}
